```rust
/// `text` as notation that types it literally, as Vim's and Evil's `@` do: `<` becomes
/// `<lt>`, a newline `<NL>` (Ctrl-J), a carriage return `<CR>`, a tab `<Tab>`, ESC
/// `<Esc>`, and any other C0 character `<C-x>` for its letter.
pub fn escape_notation(text: &str) -> String {
    let mut s = String::new();
    for c in text.chars() {
        match c {
            '<' => s.push_str("<lt>"),
            '\n' => s.push_str("<NL>"),
            '\r' => s.push_str("<CR>"),
            '\t' => s.push_str("<Tab>"),
            '\x1b' => s.push_str("<Esc>"),
            c if (c as u32) < 0x20 => s.push_str(&format!("<C-{}>", ((c as u8) + b'`') as char)),
            c => s.push(c),
        }
    }
    s
}
```
The Register field is K6's ("typed registers"), so add it there, before any struct literal is built outside core.
